# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Cheuk Hin Ho et al. (2026). Flexible uncertainty calibration for machine-learned interatomic potentials.
#   npj Computational Materials. doi:10.1038/s41524-026-02080-3  arXiv:2510.00721v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2510.00721v1 (sha256 c4640c42a611db6c...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 151 (Training/reliability). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: bibliographic facts only. The paper proposes a
# calibration of per-atom force uncertainties (conformal prediction with
# a learned, environment-dependent quantile model) and tests it on the
# pretrained MACE-MP-0b3 foundation model for LiCl, catalytic surfaces,
# MPtraj, MatPES and cross-functional transfer. Its results are
# error-uncertainty correlations and detection rates, not accuracy
# metrics of a potential. Read from the arXiv preprint (v1).

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
